  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ERNEST BEUTLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ernest Beutler was a hematologist and poet who passed away at the age of 80, as reported in a New York Times article."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ernest Beutler was an American hematologist and medical researcher who made significant contributions to the field of hematology, particularly in the area of red blood cell metabolism and disorders."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHICAGO, ILLINOIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chicago, Illinois is the birthplace of Ernest Beutler and the location where he received his undergraduate degree from the University of Chicago."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CHICAGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Chicago is the institution where Ernest Beutler received both his undergraduate degree and his medical degree."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CHICAGO PRITZKER SCHOOL OF MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Chicago Pritzker School of Medicine is the institution where Ernest Beutler earned his medical degree in 1952."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL INSTITUTES OF HEALTH (NIH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Institutes of Health (NIH) is the institution where Ernest Beutler served as a research associate."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA, SAN DIEGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of California, San Diego is the institution where Ernest Beutler joined the faculty and established the Division of Hematology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANADA GAIRDNER INTERNATIONAL AWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Canada Gairdner International Award is a prestigious award that recognizes outstanding contributions to medical science, which Ernest Beutler received in 1975."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIAN\/PACIFIC AMERICAN AWARDS FOR LITERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Asian\/Pacific American Awards for Literature is a prestigious award recognizing outstanding literary works by Asian\/Pacific American authors, which Ernest Beutler received in 1995."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED BLOOD CELL METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red blood cell metabolism is a focus of Ernest Beutler's research, particularly in the context of disorders such as G6PD deficiency and pyruvate kinase deficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G6PD DEFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G6PD deficiency is a disorder studied by Ernest Beutler, contributing to the understanding and development of diagnostic tests and treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRUVATE KINASE DEFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyruvate kinase deficiency is another disorder studied by Ernest Beutler, contributing to the understanding and development of diagnostic tests and treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnostic tests are part of Ernest Beutler's contributions to the field of hematology, specifically for disorders like G6PD deficiency and pyruvate kinase deficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatments for blood disorders are part of Ernest Beutler's contributions to the field of hematology, specifically for disorders like G6PD deficiency and pyruvate kinase deficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD DISORDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood disorders are a focus of Ernest Beutler's research, particularly in the context of red blood cell metabolism and the development of diagnostic tests and treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medicine is the field in which Ernest Beutler made significant contributions, particularly in the area of hematology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Science is the field in which Ernest Beutler made significant contributions, particularly in the area of hematology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMANITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Humanity is the subject of Ernest Beutler's contributions, particularly in the context of understanding and treating blood disorders."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICINE, SCIENCE, AND THE HUMAN EXPERIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ernest Beutler's literary works often explored themes of medicine, science, and the human experience."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE BLOOD OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Blood of Life is a poetry collection by Ernest Beutler that won the Asian\/Pacific American Awards for Literature in 1995."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOLOGIST AND POET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematologist and Poet describes Ernest Beutler's dual professional and creative roles."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0385</data>
    </node>
